# .reviewignore — paths the review engine must never review.
#
# gitignore syntax (same as .gitignore, including `!` negation and directory
# patterns). Consumed by the `review` MCP ops when resolving a scope: any path
# matched here is dropped from the reviewed file set. Your repo's .gitignore is
# honored on top of this, so gitignored files are never reviewed either.
#
# Auto-generated on the first review; edit freely — it is never overwritten.
.kanban/

# The upstream files of the local tree-sitter grammar targets (git.md,
# decision 12). They are the files of an upstream tag with no change, thus a
# review finding in them has no fix in this repository. The files that this
# repository writes in those targets (for example `scanner_build.c`) stay in
# the review.
Sources/TreeSitterJavaScript/src/
Sources/TreeSitterJavaScript/include/
Sources/TreeSitterJavaScript/LICENSE
Sources/TreeSitterPython/src/
Sources/TreeSitterPython/include/
Sources/TreeSitterPython/LICENSE
